# Claude Code Configuration

## Project Context

This is the elevai-connect Amazon Connect Pulumi infrastructure project. Always read CLAUDE.md for critical safety rules before making any deployments or configuration changes.

## Available Workshops

Users can work through the following workshops located in the `workshops/` directory:

### 1. Amazon Q Knowledge Base Setup
**Location:** `workshops/q-knowledgebase-set-up/`
**Description:** Step-by-step guide to set up Amazon Q in Connect with document ingestion, tagging, and Lex bot integration.

**Workshop includes:**
- Document upload instructions
- Lex bot creation
- Contact flow import
- Testing procedures
- Sample PDF documents and metadata files

**To start this workshop:** Read `workshops/q-knowledgebase-set-up/README.md`

## Key Files to Reference

- `CLAUDE.md` - **READ THIS FIRST** - Contains critical safety rules
- `Pulumi.*.yaml` - Stack configuration files
- `custom/` - Directory for user extensions (safe to modify)
- `core/` - Core infrastructure (do not modify)

## Important Reminders

⚠️ **CRITICAL:**
- Always use `pulumi preview` (bash) before deployments
- Use MCP tool `pulumi_up` for actual deployments
- Use MCP tool `update_stack_config` for configuration changes
- NEVER modify files in `core/` directory
- Add custom code only to `custom/` directory